# Merge behaviour for the AI memory layer.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Parallel `/orchestrate` runs build on separate `orch-<id>` branches, and every one
# of them ends with a memory-reflection pass that appends a new entry to
# .agents/memory/errors.md (or a sibling log). `/orchestrate --integrate` then merges
# those branches LOCALLY (git merge --no-ff — see .agents/reference/parallel-orchestration.md).
# Two branches appending to the same log touch the same hunk, so without `union` that
# is a guaranteed conflict — on a file where both sides are correct and the right
# resolution is always "keep both".
#
# `union` is a BUILT-IN git merge driver: for a region both sides changed it emits
# both sides' lines instead of conflict markers. Nothing needs to be configured
# per-clone for it to work.

# Normalise line endings: mixed CRLF/LF clones churn every diff (seen on Windows
# checkouts downstream). First rule on purpose — later `merge=` lines stack on top.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Append-only logs: keep both sides ----------------------------------------
# Note `*` does not cross `/`, so the direct children, domain/ and archive/ each
# need their own line.
.agents/memory/*.md         merge=union
.agents/memory/domain/*.md  merge=union
.agents/memory/archive/**   merge=union

# --- Exclusions: this block is a SAFETY BOUNDARY, not tidiness -----------------
# `union` emits NO conflict markers. On a file that is edited or regenerated in
# place, a line changed differently on two branches is duplicated SILENTLY, with
# nothing to flag it. These files are exactly that, so they must keep git's normal
# 3-way merge:
#   - index.md, reflection-protocol.md      edited in place
#   - architecture.md, project-brief.md,
#     domain/business-model.md              regenerated wholesale (.agents/memory/index.md)
#   - user-profile.md                       gitignored; listed so the intent survives
#
# `!merge` (Unspecified) is required here. `-merge` (Unset) is NOT the same thing —
# it makes git treat the path as binary and refuse to merge content at all.
# These lines must stay BELOW the rules above: a later match wins.
.agents/memory/index.md                 !merge
.agents/memory/reflection-protocol.md   !merge
.agents/memory/architecture.md          !merge
.agents/memory/project-brief.md         !merge
.agents/memory/domain/business-model.md !merge
.agents/memory/user-profile.md          !merge

# Adding a new REGENERATED file under domain/? Add it to the block above, or the
# `domain/*.md` rule sweeps it into the union set and its rewrites merge silently.
#
# A domain/ PLACEHOLDER (frontmatter `status: empty`) is union-merged too, and its
# FIRST population is an in-place rewrite of that frontmatter — two branches doing
# it concurrently merge into corrupt frontmatter with exit 0. Populate a placeholder
# only on an up-to-date branch and merge that commit alone — see
# .agents/memory/reflection-protocol.md ("These log files carry merge=union").
